Subject: [PATCH] Link GPU LLVM libraries only for enabled backends

Upstream-Reference: https://github.com/triton-lang/triton/tree/v3.8.0
Upstream-Status: Downstream

The RISC-V CPU-only build configures LLVM with RISCV and X86 targets and
leaves TRITON_CODEGEN_BACKENDS empty. Link each GPU LLVM library group only
when its matching backend is enabled.
---
 CMakeLists.txt | 9 +++++++--
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/CMakeLists.txt b/CMakeLists.txt
index 3f066ea..6e105eb 100644
--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -374,12 +374,19 @@ if(TRITON_BUILD_PYTHON_MODULE)
     # LLVM
     LLVMPasses
-    LLVMNVPTXCodeGen
-    LLVMAMDGPUCodeGen
-    LLVMAMDGPUAsmParser
-
     Python3::Module
     pybind11::headers
   )
+  if("nvidia" IN_LIST TRITON_CODEGEN_BACKENDS)
+    list(APPEND TRITON_LIBRARIES
+      LLVMNVPTXCodeGen
+    )
+  endif()
+  if("amd" IN_LIST TRITON_CODEGEN_BACKENDS)
+    list(APPEND TRITON_LIBRARIES
+      LLVMAMDGPUCodeGen
+      LLVMAMDGPUAsmParser
+    )
+  endif()
   if(CMAKE_SYSTEM_PROCESSOR MATCHES "aarch64" OR # Linux arm64
      CMAKE_SYSTEM_PROCESSOR MATCHES "arm64" OR # macOS arm64
      CMAKE_OSX_ARCHITECTURES MATCHES "arm64")  # also macOS arm64
